# Per-machine zsh overrides — sourced from ~/.zshrc near the end.
#
# Written by chezmoi whenever it is missing (the `create_` source-state
# attribute) and never overwritten — your edits here are durable. Undo an
# override by commenting it out: an empty file counts as removed, and a
# non-interactive apply then stops on it.
#
# Use for things that aren't portable:
#   - per-machine secrets / tokens (prefer 1Password or an `op run` wrapper)
#   - hostname-specific aliases / functions
#   - PATH additions for tools installed outside mise / brew
#   - SSH_AUTH_SOCK overrides
#   - work-only env vars (HTTP_PROXY, CORP_VPN_HOST)
#
# Examples (uncomment + edit):
#
# alias k=kubectl
# export PATH="/opt/local-tool/bin:$PATH"
